# PR opened — agent checklist (DocCy)

When the user says they opened / created / pushed a PR (or asks to watch CI on a new PR), do this **in chat** every time. Do **not** rely on GitHub PR description checkboxes for these reminders — the user reads those too late.

## 1. Local register gate (not CI)

Immediately remind them to run once on the testing DB:

```bash
npm run test:e2e:register
```

Live `/register` (Places/Auth/Resend), founder email asserted, doctor deleted afterwards. See `docs/ci-test-policy.md`.

Then **ask** whether they want you to run it for them in this session. Do not start it until they say yes.

Do **not** add this block back into PR body templates as the primary reminder path.

## 2. Watch CI and fix failures

Stay on the PR checks. If any fail, diagnose and fix (push to the PR branch). Prefer fixing real product/test mismatches over blind re-runs.

## 3. Master / coworker sync (Livio)

Coworker: **Livio** (`elance1985`, typically `liviolanzo@gmail.com`).

After `git fetch origin master`, report whether this branch is behind `origin/master` (commits not yet in the PR). Call out Livio’s commits explicitly when present. Ask before merging/rebasing master into the PR branch unless the user already asked to update from master.
